{"term":"tsunami","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:97a771919d3ce9f715","definition":"A very large and destructive wave, generally caused by a tremendous disturbance in the ocean, such as an undersea earthquake or volcanic eruption; often a series of waves (a wave train).","example":"A tsunami struck Japan recently.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["seismic sea wave","tidal wave"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["flunami","fog tsunami","ice tsunami","megatsunami","meteotsunami","orphaned tsunami","palaeotsunami","paleotsunami","poonami","silver tsunami","teletsunami","tsunameter","tsunamic","tsunamigenic","tsunamilike","tsunami stone","tsunami wall"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tsunami#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0aceddb05f2ebc73db","definition":"A large and generally unstoppable surge.","example":"It seemed that what started out as a handful of isolated cases gradually turned into a tsunami of complaints.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["seismic sea wave","tidal wave"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["flunami","fog tsunami","ice tsunami","megatsunami","meteotsunami","orphaned tsunami","palaeotsunami","paleotsunami","poonami","silver tsunami","teletsunami","tsunameter","tsunamic","tsunamigenic","tsunamilike","tsunami stone","tsunami wall"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tsunami#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/(t)suːˈnɑːmi/"},"wordFamily":["flunami","fog tsunami","ice tsunami","megatsunami","meteotsunami","orphaned tsunami","palaeotsunami","paleotsunami","poonami","silver tsunami","teletsunami","tsunameter","tsunamic","tsunamigenic","tsunamilike","tsunami stone","tsunami wall"]}